    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d261">

                <pb facs="0326" n="316" xml:id="pg316"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Germany)/5–2945:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-29T21:00:00+02:00">May 29, 1945—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3066. The substance of the Dep’s 2351,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d261-f1"/> May 28 in
                    memo form was conveyed to Chauvel<anchor n="4" xml:id="d261-f2"/> this afternoon
                    who promised that he would bring it personally to the attention of Bidault this
                    evening. He added that he heartily approves of the action we propose to take in
                    this regard and will recommend that the French Govt send similar instructions to
                    Massigli. He added that our communication might hasten the announcement of the
                    French member of the German Control Commission. He concluded by warning,
                    however, that the final decision would, of course, rest with de Gaulle.</p>
                <p>Sent Dept 3066; rptd London 361 and Moscow 93.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d261-f1" n="3" xml:id="d261-f1-content">
                <p>Same as Department’s telegram 4216, May 26, to London, <ref target="#pg308">p.
                        308</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d261-f2" n="4" xml:id="d261-f2-content">
                <p>Jean Chauvel, Secretary General of the French Ministry for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
